<!--
  BUG FIXED / FEATURE ADDED ("إشعارات أكثر تطوراً"): every notification in
  NotificationHelper.kt used to call setSmallIcon(android.R.drawable.ic_popup_reminder)
  - a generic Android system "reminder" bell that ships with the OS itself,
  not anything belonging to this app. In the status bar and notification
  shade that shows up as an unbranded, generic-looking icon no different
  from a dozen other apps, instead of something recognizably "shop
  manager". Per Android's own notification-icon guidelines, the status-bar
  icon must be a flat, single-color (white) silhouette with a transparent
  background - the system tints/masks it itself (and on API 21+ draws it
  inside a colored circle using the notification's accent color) - so this
  is a plain shopping-bag silhouette rather than a colored/detailed image.
-->
